## Approved Strategic Priorities

### Priority 1: Execute Growth Plan

**Board Expectation:** Deliver 12% revenue CAGR to achieve $15B by 2030

| Metric | FY2026 Target | 5-Year Target |
|--------|---------------|---------------|
| Revenue | $9.2-9.5B | $15.0B |
| Operating Margin | 12.5-13.0% | 16.0% |
| EPS | $4.75-5.00 | $10.50 |

**Board Oversight:**
- Quarterly progress reviews
- Annual strategy session
- Investment approval per policy

### Priority 2: Maintain Innovation Leadership

**Board Expectation:** Sustain R&D investment at 11%+ of revenue

| Metric | FY2026 Target |
|--------|---------------|
| R&D Investment | $1.05B+ |
| Patents Filed | 75+ |
| New Product Revenue | 24%+ |

**Board Oversight:**
- Technology Committee review (quarterly)
- Major program milestones
- IP portfolio review (annual)

### Priority 3: Drive Operational Excellence

**Board Expectation:** Expand operating margin by 100 bps annually

| Initiative | FY2026 Target |
|------------|---------------|
| Manufacturing Productivity | +5% |
| Digital Transformation | Per roadmap |
| Supply Chain Efficiency | 3% cost reduction |

**Board Oversight:**
- Monthly financial review
- Quarterly operating review
- Annual efficiency assessment

### Priority 4: Execute Sustainability Commitments

**Board Expectation:** Achieve 2030 carbon neutrality goal

| Metric | FY2026 Target |
|--------|---------------|
| Scope 1+2 Emissions | -15% |
| Renewable Energy | 78% |
| Sustainability Investment | $55M |

**Board Oversight:**
- ESG Committee review (quarterly)
- CDP/sustainability reporting
- Annual ESG strategy session

### Priority 5: Strengthen Talent and Culture

**Board Expectation:** Top-quartile employee engagement

| Metric | FY2026 Target |
|--------|---------------|
| Employee Engagement | 78% favorable |
| Diversity (Leadership) | 40% |
| Voluntary Turnover | <8% |

**Board Oversight:**
- Compensation Committee review
- Annual talent review
- Culture assessment

